Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdkfd: BC-250/gfx1013 — flush the compute TLB by
 rebuilding the runlist

The compute TLB on this board is never invalidated.
gmc_v10_0_flush_gpu_tlb_pasid() looks for the VMID that owns the PASID in
mmATC_VMID*_PASID_MAPPING, a register that on gfx10 under HWS is never
written -- measured as 20 of 20 flushes hitting zero VMIDs, reproduced on
separate hardware. Forcing the invalidation through MMIO does not work: the
attempt wedges the translation unit and resets the GPU.

Measured consequence: hipFree unmaps, hipMalloc reuses the same VA with a new
physical address, the new PTEs are correct in memory, and the GPU keeps
translating through the previous mapping (15 of 15 failing pages across 3 runs
pointed at exactly the VA's earlier generation). An invalidation that works
does exist: activating a second process makes the firmware preempt the queues,
rebuild the runlist and reassign VMIDs. This patch asks for that cycle on
unmap. 36 counterbalanced runs, single boot: stock 13/18 dirty, runlist 0/18
dirty, Fisher p = 3.7e-06. Verified active by ftrace execute_queues_cpsch
counts (6 -> 68), zero board errors.

Safety: takes dqm_lock, so kfd_flush_tlb() must not call it. Only call site is
the unmap ioctl in kfd_chardev.c (p->mutex held, dqm_lock free).

Deployed form: this file reproduces, byte for byte, the build2 tree shipped on
blade 15 (a fleet blade, snapshot snap-8fe794e8, "25-patch (GabriWar): fix
aliasing — flush TLB via runlist rebuild", module amdgpu.ko srcversion
C484A6D2). Differences from GabriWar's upstream
bc250-rocm-gabriwar/patches/bc250-flush-tlb-by-runlist.patch (cec746e):
- upstream gates the call on `if (flush_tlb)`; the deployed tree calls it
  unconditionally on unmap
- upstream places the param block next to the function; the deployed tree puts
  it near the top of kfd_device_queue_manager.c
- the <linux/module.h> include is carried by patch 19 here (single addition in
  the deployed tree)
- MODULE_PARM_DESC wording is the deployed English translation

Off by default: amdgpu.bc250_flush_by_runlist=1. The suite arms it in
/etc/modprobe.d/aputune-40cu.conf during `aputune build --run` (deployed blades
carry the same line as /etc/modprobe.d/bc250-runlist.conf).

By Gabriel Duarte Guerra (GabriWar).
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/kfd_device_queue_manager.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/kfd_device_queue_manager.c
@@ -50,6 +50,28 @@
 static int set_pasid_vmid_mapping(struct device_queue_manager *dqm,
 				  u32 pasid, unsigned int vmid);
 
+/* BC-250/gfx1013: invalidate the compute TLB by rebuilding the runlist.
+ *
+ * The compute TLB on this board is never invalidated.
+ * gmc_v10_0_flush_gpu_tlb_pasid() searches mmATC_VMID*_PASID_MAPPING,
+ * a register that on gfx10 under HWS is never written -- measured as
+ * 20 of 20 flushes hitting zero VMIDs. Forcing it through MMIO does
+ * not work: neither KIQ nor direct register is acknowledged.
+ *
+ * What does work: the hardware scheduler rebuilds the runlist when
+ * activating another process, and must invalidate the TLB at that
+ * point or the new process would inherit stale translations.
+ * Ask for that cycle on unmap so the stale entry never survives.
+ *
+ * Takes dqm_lock. Never call from kfd_flush_tlb() -- deadlock.
+ * Only call site is the unmap ioctl (holds p->mutex, not dqm_lock).
+ */
+
+static int bc250_flush_by_runlist;
+module_param(bc250_flush_by_runlist, int, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(bc250_flush_by_runlist,
+       "BC-250: flush compute TLB by rebuilding the runlist on unmap (0=off, 1=on)");
+
 static int execute_queues_cpsch(struct device_queue_manager *dqm,
 				enum kfd_unmap_queues_filter filter,
 				uint32_t filter_param,
@@ -2126,6 +2148,51 @@
 }
 
 /* dqm->lock mutex has to be locked before calling this function */
+/* BC-250/gfx1013: invalidate the compute TLB by rebuilding the runlist.
+ *
+ * The compute TLB on this board is never invalidated.
+ * gmc_v10_0_flush_gpu_tlb_pasid() searches mmATC_VMID*_PASID_MAPPING,
+ * a register that on gfx10 under HWS is never written -- measured as
+ * 20 of 20 flushes hitting zero VMIDs. Forcing it through MMIO does
+ * not work: neither KIQ nor direct register is acknowledged.
+ *
+ * What does work: the hardware scheduler rebuilds the runlist when
+ * activating another process, and must invalidate the TLB at that
+ * point or the new process would inherit stale translations.
+ * Ask for that cycle on unmap so the stale entry never survives.
+ *
+ * Takes dqm_lock. Never call from kfd_flush_tlb() -- deadlock.
+ */
+
+/* See the long comment above bc250_flush_by_runlist. */
+int kfd_bc250_flush_by_runlist(struct kfd_node *dev)
+{
+       struct device_queue_manager *dqm;
+       int r;
+
+       if (!bc250_flush_by_runlist || !dev || !dev->adev || !dev->adev->pdev)
+               return 0;
+       if (dev->adev->pdev->device != BC250_PCI_DEVICE_ID)
+               return 0;
+
+       dqm = dev->dqm;
+       /* Only meaningful under hardware scheduling: the firmware
+        * reassigns VMIDs when rebuilding the runlist.
+        */
+       if (!dqm || dqm->sched_policy == KFD_SCHED_POLICY_NO_HWS)
+               return 0;
+
+       dqm_lock(dqm);
+       r = execute_queues_cpsch(dqm, KFD_UNMAP_QUEUES_FILTER_DYNAMIC_QUEUES, 0,
+                                USE_DEFAULT_GRACE_PERIOD);
+       dqm_unlock(dqm);
+
+       if (r)
+               dev_err_ratelimited(dev->adev->dev,
+                       "BC-250: runlist rebuild failed (%d)\n", r);
+       return r;
+}
+
 static int map_queues_cpsch(struct device_queue_manager *dqm)
 {
 	struct device *dev = dqm->dev->adev->dev;
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/kfd_chardev.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/kfd_chardev.c
@@ -1458,6 +1458,9 @@
 			kfd_flush_tlb(peer_pdd);
 
 		/* Remove dma mapping after tlb flush to avoid IO_PAGE_FAULT */
+                       /* BC-250: rebuild runlist to flush stale TLB entries */
+                       kfd_bc250_flush_by_runlist(peer_pdd->dev);
+
 		err = amdgpu_amdkfd_gpuvm_dmaunmap_mem(mem, peer_pdd->drm_priv);
 		if (err)
 			goto sync_memory_failed;
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/kfd_device_queue_manager.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/kfd_device_queue_manager.h
@@ -372,3 +372,9 @@
 
 
 #endif /* KFD_DEVICE_QUEUE_MANAGER_H_ */
+
+/* BC-250: rebuild the runlist so the firmware invalidates the compute TLB.
+ * Full documentation in kfd_device_queue_manager.c above bc250_flush_by_runlist.
+ * Takes dqm_lock -- never call while already holding it.
+ */
+int kfd_bc250_flush_by_runlist(struct kfd_node *dev);
